  "analysis": "Round 1 showed small scale (0.3-0.7) is the dominant lever: patches jumped 0.713->0.791, but inclusion stayed flat (0.355) and scratches dropped 0.714->0.667. Miss analysis of the kept model: inclusion misses are overwhelmingly tiny (median 33.8px vs 90.5px train; 146/179 in low tertile, recall 0.178) - the 0.3-0.7 pastes (~27-63px) are still larger than the missed median, so inclusion may need even smaller pastes (0.3-0.5 -> ~27-45px). Inclusion may also be data-starved (10 real images) - round 1's inclusion-heavy test was confounded by default scale, so retest allocation at the known-good small scale. Scratches: the 0.047 AP drop vs control exceeds the noise band, suggesting small pastes of thin lines hurt; missed scratches (median 41.8px) sit between the two tested ranges, so probe a mid scale 0.5-1.0. Three one-factor tests vs the kept plan: (1) inclusion scale 0.3-0.5, (2) inclusion-heavy allocation 24/13/13, (3) scratch scale 0.5-1.0. All keep same_class pool (any_class hurt inclusion badly in R1).",
