      }
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Scratch AP fell 0.714->0.667 when pastes shrank to 0.3-0.7 (beyond the ~0.03 noise band), suggesting very small thin-line pastes are unlearnable noise, yet missed scratches (median 41.8px) are small. A mid scale 0.5-1.0 (~36-73px from ~73px sources) should recover scratch AP50 toward ~0.71 while keeping patches/inclusion at their proven 0.3-0.7; if scratches do not recover, the R1 drop was noise and per-class scale tuning is unnecessary.",
